WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.640
Yeah, so this is a this is one of the

00:00:01.720 --> 00:00:05.280
stories in the book that I think will be

00:00:03.640 --> 00:00:07.400
impactful and I tell almost all these

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:11.960
stories in the book. Um

00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:14.560
but the I was probably this was 2015.

00:00:11.960 --> 00:00:16.520
I had made we had our first really good

00:00:14.560 --> 00:00:18.400
year. 2015 was our first really good

00:00:16.520 --> 00:00:19.720
storage season and we found ourselves

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:21.880
sitting on

00:00:19.720 --> 00:00:23.640
600k of cash that we'd saved up over the

00:00:21.880 --> 00:00:25.200
over the previous years in business. We

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:26.480
found ourselves

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:28.120
um

00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:29.760
you know, about to do a self-storage

00:00:28.120 --> 00:00:31.400
development.

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:33.800
We just had a lot going on and a little

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:35.480
bit of money. Um

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:36.560
my buddy who's in who's a mentor of

00:00:35.480 --> 00:00:38.680
mine, he's

00:00:36.560 --> 00:00:40.800
15 years older than me.

00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:42.160
He lives in DC. He's a wealth manager.

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:44.960
His name's Jim.

00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:46.520
Um he called me into a

00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:47.600
my my wife and his wife are best

00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:49.160
friends. He called me into his office.

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:50.360
He's like, "Hey, let's do a like let's

00:00:49.160 --> 00:00:52.000
do a rundown. Like I want to just make

00:00:50.360 --> 00:00:54.400
make sure you're in a good spot."

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:56.040
He sits me down in his office at his at

00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:57.520
his in his

00:00:56.040 --> 00:00:59.040
you know, three-story building in

00:00:57.520 --> 00:01:00.320
Reston, Mass.

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:02.360
Where we he's he's got the whole top

00:01:00.320 --> 00:01:03.800
floor. He's got 60 employees in there.

00:01:02.360 --> 00:01:05.440
We scoot right through with the guy who

00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:07.760
owns the business and it turns out he

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:09.560
does this with all new clients. We go

00:01:07.760 --> 00:01:11.440
into the biggest conference room

00:01:09.560 --> 00:01:13.040
and he sits us down and we spend 1 hour

00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:14.880
breaking down my entire life and

00:01:13.040 --> 00:01:16.480
business and all my money, where the

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:18.720
money's coming in, what accounts it's

00:01:16.480 --> 00:01:22.160
in. And he

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:25.400
unloads more value on me in 1 hour than

00:01:22.160 --> 00:01:27.040
anybody ever has with Hey, you know, I

00:01:25.400 --> 00:01:28.040
didn't know we were in the process of

00:01:27.040 --> 00:01:29.680
building a self-storage facility. I

00:01:28.040 --> 00:01:31.480
didn't know what bonus depreciation was

00:01:29.680 --> 00:01:32.480
or cost segregation.

00:01:31.480 --> 00:01:33.280
He's like, "Hey man, you're going to get

00:01:32.480 --> 00:01:34.480
like

00:01:33.280 --> 00:01:35.960
you can get six or seven hundred

00:01:34.480 --> 00:01:37.120
thousand dollar tax write-off on this

00:01:35.960 --> 00:01:38.240
building when you're done. Like this is

00:01:37.120 --> 00:01:40.880
how you need to do it. This is who you

00:01:38.240 --> 00:01:42.280
need to like talk to. Um by the way, do

00:01:40.880 --> 00:01:43.840
you have key man insurance? What happens

00:01:42.280 --> 00:01:45.240
if your business partner passes away or

00:01:43.840 --> 00:01:46.960
you pass away? How you going to buy the

00:01:45.240 --> 00:01:47.960
other person out? It's not about like I

00:01:46.960 --> 00:01:49.240
know you guys have enough money to

00:01:47.960 --> 00:01:51.040
handle the funeral. It's not about that.

00:01:49.240 --> 00:01:52.760
Like how how is your wife going to be

00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:54.440
able to buy Danny

00:01:52.760 --> 00:01:56.320
or or uh how's Danny going to be able to

00:01:54.440 --> 00:01:58.320
buy your wife out of the business if you

00:01:56.320 --> 00:01:59.360
die? If Danny dies, how you going to be

00:01:58.320 --> 00:02:00.560
able to buy his family out of the

00:01:59.360 --> 00:02:01.440
business?

00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:02.760
Who are you going to be able to hire to

00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:04.000
replace him to run the company? Are you

00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:06.520
going to have some key man insurance on

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:08.320
that? Um and just on down the list of

00:02:06.520 --> 00:02:10.039
all the different ways

00:02:08.320 --> 00:02:11.800
that we could plan and strategize and

00:02:10.039 --> 00:02:14.120
tax, you know,

00:02:11.800 --> 00:02:16.760
just optimize for tax efficiency from

00:02:14.120 --> 00:02:17.760
being a C corp or an S corp, um you

00:02:16.760 --> 00:02:18.760
know, all the little things that we

00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:19.880
could do. So, at the end of this

00:02:18.760 --> 00:02:21.959
meeting,

00:02:19.880 --> 00:02:23.640
there's a whiteboard full

00:02:21.959 --> 00:02:25.440
of

00:02:23.640 --> 00:02:26.640
all this advice. And like it's the to-do

00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:28.360
list, basically. Nick's to-do list of

00:02:26.640 --> 00:02:29.000
bang bang bang bang bang.

00:02:28.360 --> 00:02:30.920
And

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:32.440
oddly none of it was like

00:02:30.920 --> 00:02:34.000
he didn't sell himself on any of this

00:02:32.440 --> 00:02:35.240
stuff.

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:37.000
He gives me a bunch of handouts, he

00:02:35.240 --> 00:02:39.400
takes a picture of the whiteboard, and

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:41.040
he says, "Okay, like

00:02:39.400 --> 00:02:42.520
we're done here." And I'm like, "Hold

00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:44.120
on, Jim. Like

00:02:42.520 --> 00:02:46.360
send me an invoice. Like what is this

00:02:44.120 --> 00:02:48.120
normally What do you normally charge

00:02:46.360 --> 00:02:49.600
somebody to do this?"

00:02:48.120 --> 00:02:51.880
And he goes, "Oh, Nick, you got it all

00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:54.720
wrong. Like I do this for free for all

00:02:51.880 --> 00:02:54.720
potential clients.

00:02:54.760 --> 00:02:57.440
And I'm like, "Okay, like I'm here

00:02:55.880 --> 00:02:59.120
visiting, our wives are best friends, we

00:02:57.440 --> 00:03:01.239
drank 20 Coors Lights last night. Like I

00:02:59.120 --> 00:03:02.239
understand why you did it for me.

00:03:01.239 --> 00:03:03.400
But like

00:03:02.239 --> 00:03:05.680
how in the world does it make sense for

00:03:03.400 --> 00:03:07.760
you to spend an hour and do this for all

00:03:05.680 --> 00:03:08.720
the other people?" And he goes,

00:03:07.760 --> 00:03:11.239
"Nick, do you realize the people that

00:03:08.720 --> 00:03:13.920
come in here and sit in my office?

00:03:11.239 --> 00:03:15.640
Like they have business problems. Which

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:17.640
guess what that means, Nick?

00:03:15.640 --> 00:03:20.160
They have money. They have influence.

00:03:17.640 --> 00:03:21.880
They have a lot of things going on.

00:03:20.160 --> 00:03:23.200
They are high-powered individuals. They

00:03:21.880 --> 00:03:24.560
are, you know, if I were going to rate

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:27.200
my clients from one to five, they're the

00:03:24.560 --> 00:03:27.200
fives.

00:03:27.239 --> 00:03:30.239
So, I don't send them an invoice on the

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:31.239
first meeting. I don't talk about money

00:03:30.239 --> 00:03:32.680
on the first meeting. I don't sell

00:03:31.239 --> 00:03:35.080
myself on the first meeting. I build

00:03:32.680 --> 00:03:35.800
trust with them. And guess what, Nick?

00:03:35.080 --> 00:03:37.959
Like

00:03:35.800 --> 00:03:41.239
30 40% of them sign up with me and move

00:03:37.959 --> 00:03:42.480
money to me on the spot.

00:03:41.239 --> 00:03:43.880
And he's like, "The rest of them call me

00:03:42.480 --> 00:03:45.440
6 months later when they have another

00:03:43.880 --> 00:03:46.480
business problem, and they become my

00:03:45.440 --> 00:03:49.160
client, and we enter a paid

00:03:46.480 --> 00:03:50.400
relationship. Because I build the trust,

00:03:49.160 --> 00:03:52.080
and because I add the value to their

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:54.520
lives."

00:03:52.080 --> 00:03:55.800
And my mind exploded, and it changed the

00:03:54.520 --> 00:03:57.080
way I think about everything. Now, not

00:03:55.800 --> 00:03:59.080
every sales environment you can apply

00:03:57.080 --> 00:04:01.120
that to. It's not a sales strategy you

00:03:59.080 --> 00:04:02.520
can use for everything. People will walk

00:04:01.120 --> 00:04:04.800
all over you. You will waste time. You

00:04:02.520 --> 00:04:06.920
got to be really careful about that.

00:04:04.800 --> 00:04:08.360
But in certain situations, like proving

00:04:06.920 --> 00:04:11.600
you're an expert, building trust, and

00:04:08.360 --> 00:04:13.360
adding as much value as possible,

00:04:11.600 --> 00:04:15.760
it just comes back around. It comes back

00:04:13.360 --> 00:04:15.760
around.

